WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.419
From being
the B in apartment 23

00:00:02.503 --> 00:00:04.713
to the super-strong
Jessica Jones,

00:00:04.796 --> 00:00:06.423
Krysten Ritter is a delight

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:08.759
whatever show
or movie she's cast in.

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:10.594
And now we get to see her
try her hand

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.263
at playing an evil witch
in Netflix's Nightbooks.

00:00:13.347 --> 00:00:14.181
Boo.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:15.891
But first, let's pay tribute

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:17.768
to her incredible
career so far

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.562
and take a look
at her road to Netflix.

00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:22.564
Back to the 2000s
and to the start

00:00:22.648 --> 00:00:24.733
of Krysten's budding
acting career.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:27.152
Here she is
in a 2002 Fiat advert.

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:29.029
Then a model
signed to Wilhelmina.

00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:29.988
No big deal.

00:00:30.072 --> 00:00:31.573
She dazzled
casting directors

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:33.283
with her bubbly personality,

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.619
which made her transition
from modelling to acting

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.079
a natural fit.

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.373
Her early roles were
bit parts in film and TV,

00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:42.000
such as the role of one
of the art history students

00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:43.377
in Mona Lisa Smile.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:46.171
"Funeral Mask,"
Mycenaean, 1200.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.007
By 2005,
Krysten was popping up

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:51.218
as a recurring character
on long-running shows.

00:00:51.301 --> 00:00:53.178
From 2005 to 2006,

00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:54.721
she played Gia Goodman

00:00:54.805 --> 00:00:57.558
on the murder mystery
teen drama Veronica Mars.

00:00:57.641 --> 00:00:58.892
Her character
was the daughter

00:00:58.976 --> 00:01:00.686
of a wealthy
baseball team owner,

00:01:00.769 --> 00:01:01.687
attending Neptune High

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.689
alongside
Kristen Bell's Veronica.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:06.275
She reprised this role
in the 2014 film,

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.317
where Gia returns,

00:01:07.401 --> 00:01:09.987
now a wealthy socialite
in the frame for murder.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.530
So many mixed emotions
right now.

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.032
I kind of hated you, like
a lot, but I don't anymore.

00:01:14.116 --> 00:01:15.450
Just trying
to remember my progress,

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.286
because blaming you
for telling the whole world

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:18.829
that my dad was a paedophile

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.873
is what my therapist calls
"misplaced aggression."

00:01:20.956 --> 00:01:23.333
So, basically,
we're totally cool.

00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:25.627
Following her original stint
on Veronica Mars,

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:27.880
she appeared on another
hugely beloved show,

00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:29.339
Gilmore Girls.

00:01:29.423 --> 00:01:31.341
-Is that too much popcorn?
-Uh, yeah.

00:01:31.425 --> 00:01:32.426
I'm really hungry.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.511
Between 2006 and 2007,

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:37.472
she played one of Rory's
classmates at Yale, Lucy.

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.308
From 2008 to 2010,

00:01:39.391 --> 00:01:42.060
she cropped up in some
classic romantic comedies,

00:01:42.144 --> 00:01:44.396
from playing the goth bride
in 27 Dresses,

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:46.440
to the best friend in
Confessions of a Shopaholic,

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:47.983
and She's Out of my League.

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:49.735
Kirk, Molly's into you.

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:51.236
And here's one
you'll remember

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.738
if you're a big fan
of Gossip Girl.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.531
In 2009, there were plans

00:01:54.615 --> 00:01:56.408
for a potential spinoff
prequel series

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.160
about a young
Lily van der Woodsen's life

00:01:58.243 --> 00:01:59.369
in the 1980s.

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:01.330
An episode in the second
series of Gossip Girl

00:02:01.413 --> 00:02:02.539
served as a backdoor pilot,

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:05.375
with Krysten playing Lily's
rebellious older sister,

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:06.335
Carol Rhodes.

00:02:06.418 --> 00:02:07.836
Come on, it's us.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.255
We travel in style,
no matter how we travel.

00:02:10.339 --> 00:02:12.007
Arguably, her breakout role

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.051
was as Jane Margolis
in Breaking Bad.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.802
Because what
I know about you,

00:02:15.886 --> 00:02:17.471
high-school teacher
turned drug dealer

00:02:17.554 --> 00:02:19.389
with a brother-in-law
in the DEA,

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:21.391
that would make
one hell of a story.

00:02:21.475 --> 00:02:22.976
National news, I'll bet.

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:26.271
Do right by Jesse tonight,

00:02:26.355 --> 00:02:27.856
or I will burn you
to the ground.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.400
Jane was Jesse's neighbour
and eventual girlfriend,

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:32.194
struggling
with drug addiction.

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:35.072
Thanks to Walt, Jane dies
a pretty horrible death,

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:36.740
which had
major repercussions

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.658
on Jesse's character

00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:39.284
throughout the rest
of the series.

00:02:39.368 --> 00:02:41.411
This was Krysten's
meatiest role to date

00:02:41.495 --> 00:02:44.206
and cemented her acting
chops outside of comedy.

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:45.999
Having starred in her
fair share of romcoms,

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:49.127
Krysten decided
to write her own in 2011.

00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:51.547
Life Happens starred Krysten
in the main role of Kim,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.132
a woman who gets pregnant
after a one-night stand

00:02:54.216 --> 00:02:55.843
and becomes
a single mother still living

00:02:55.926 --> 00:02:57.052
with her two roommates.

00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:59.012
Nobody tells you
it's going to be so hard.

00:02:59.096 --> 00:03:00.472
Yes, they do, Kim.

00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:01.890
That's pretty much
all people say.

00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:04.518
In an interview, she said
she and director Kat Coiro

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.937
came up with the plot
after Kat had a baby.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.523
Staying with comedy, but
with a dash of camp horror,

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:10.899
we've got 2012's Vamps,

00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:13.569
in which Krysten starred
alongside Alicia Silverstone

00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:16.530
as two vampires trying
to stay youthful and trendy.

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:19.116
Krysten's character, Stacy,
gets herself into a pickle

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:22.119
when she finds herself
accidentally dating the son

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:26.081
of none other than legendary
vampire hunter Van Helsing.

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:29.376
-He's goofy but cute.
-What's his name?

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:31.003
His name is Joey…

00:03:31.086 --> 00:03:32.337
Van Helsing.

00:03:32.421 --> 00:03:33.255
What?

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:35.090
Don't Trust the B----
in Apartment 23

00:03:35.174 --> 00:03:38.177
saw Krysten play wild
New York party girl Chloe,

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.179
next to Dreama Walker's
idealistic June,

00:03:40.262 --> 00:03:41.763
in an odd couple sitcom

00:03:41.847 --> 00:03:43.432
about an unlikely
friendship.

00:03:43.515 --> 00:03:45.851
Fun fact, Dawson Creek's
James van der Beek

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.019
also starred in the show

00:03:47.102 --> 00:03:49.104
as a fictionalised
version of himself.

00:03:49.188 --> 00:03:50.272
I'm gonna send this.

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:51.940
-To who?
-Everyone.

00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:54.651
Krysten's Chloe
was the perfect vehicle

00:03:54.735 --> 00:03:56.195
for her comedic talents,

00:03:56.278 --> 00:03:57.321
a character who was lovable

00:03:57.404 --> 00:03:59.448
despite being
completely irresponsible.

00:03:59.531 --> 00:04:01.617
While the show was cancelled
after two seasons,

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.202
it proved popular with fans,

00:04:03.285 --> 00:04:04.578
who have even
set up petitions

00:04:04.661 --> 00:04:05.871
for it to be renewed,

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:08.165
and was nominated for
a few Teen Choice Awards.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:11.710
On to 2014, and Krysten had
a whole host of movie roles.

00:04:11.793 --> 00:04:13.170
But her biggest film
that year

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.796
was Tim Burton's Big Eyes.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.173
It dramatizes the life

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.883
of American artist
Margaret Keane,

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:20.093
whose famed paintings
of characters with big eyes

00:04:20.177 --> 00:04:22.596
were initially attributed
to her husband.

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:25.557
Playing the outspoken Diane,
Krysten fulfilled her goal

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:28.101
of working on a Tim Burton
movie with this role,

00:04:28.185 --> 00:04:30.437
telling Nylon it was
"a total dream come true."

00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:32.606
Strange, you know,

00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:34.191
Walter doesn't
really strike me

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.943
as a cute,
hungry kitten type.

00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:37.152
And in 2015,

00:04:37.236 --> 00:04:39.738
we got to see Krysten on
Netflix for the first time

00:04:39.821 --> 00:04:42.241
as the incomparable
Jessica Jones.

00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:44.910
In this role, her star power
was fully realised

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:46.995
as the conflicted,
hard-drinking and, well,

00:04:47.079 --> 00:04:49.039
hard-hitting
former superhero.

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.082
Starring alongside

00:04:50.165 --> 00:04:52.167
David Tennant's
terrifying Kilgrave,

00:04:52.251 --> 00:04:53.544
Krysten got rave reviews

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:55.796
for her work
on the Marvel series,

00:04:55.879 --> 00:04:58.590
which explored themes like
sexual assault and PTSD.

00:04:58.674 --> 00:04:59.842
Come back here!

00:05:00.551 --> 00:05:01.552
Whoa.

00:05:01.635 --> 00:05:03.595
She also directed an episode

00:05:03.679 --> 00:05:05.347
in the final series
of the show.

00:05:05.848 --> 00:05:08.016
In 2017, she starred
in The Defenders,

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.977
where Jessica Jones teams up
with Luke Cage,

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.770
Iron Fist and Daredevil.

00:05:12.271 --> 00:05:14.147
Bullet-proof. Blind ninja.

00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.774
-Whatever it is you are.
-Classy.

00:05:15.858 --> 00:05:17.943
Another Netflix role
she reprised

00:05:18.026 --> 00:05:19.695
was that of Jane
from Breaking Bad,

00:05:19.778 --> 00:05:21.321
in a surprise
flashback cameo

00:05:21.405 --> 00:05:23.740
at the end of 2019's
El Camino.

00:05:23.824 --> 00:05:26.201
I've gone where the universe
takes me my whole life.

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:31.582
It's better to make those
decisions for yourself.

00:05:31.665 --> 00:05:32.875
That brings us to 2021

00:05:32.958 --> 00:05:36.086
and Krysten's latest
Netflix project, Nightbooks.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.213
This time she gets to play
a villain as a witch

00:05:38.297 --> 00:05:40.757
who takes a young boy
named Alex prisoner.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.218
In order to save his life,
he convinces her

00:05:43.302 --> 00:05:46.305
to let him write a scary
story for her each night.

00:05:46.388 --> 00:05:47.472
Did you say…

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.892
scary stories?

00:05:49.975 --> 00:05:51.101
But at the same time,

00:05:51.185 --> 00:05:53.061
he teams up with
another prisoner to try

00:05:53.145 --> 00:05:55.439
and figure out a way
to escape her clutches.

00:05:55.522 --> 00:05:59.318
This will hurt you far more
than it hurts me.

00:05:59.401 --> 00:06:01.153
Make sure
you don't miss Nightbooks,

00:06:01.236 --> 00:06:02.237
now streaming on Netflix.

00:06:02.821 --> 00:06:04.114
And for more
on your favourite

00:06:04.198 --> 00:06:05.532
actress trajectories
to Netflix

00:06:05.616 --> 00:06:08.493
and the stories behind your
favourite shows and movies,

00:06:08.577 --> 00:06:10.245
make sure you subscribe
to the channel.

00:06:10.329 --> 00:06:11.830
What is that?

00:06:12.873 --> 00:06:13.707
Read.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:14.958
Now.

